  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Inscr.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIEg">II Eg</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Inscr." corresp="#wit-d">Her is Eadgares cynincges gerædnes.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">Her is Eadgares cynincges gerædnes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">Here is King Edgar's ordinance.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(Hier ist König Eadgars Verordnung. D)</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Here is King Edgar's ordinance. D)</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="340"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_7">VIII Atr 7–8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="355"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-062">Cn 1018 25–27</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Heading only in D (in red; added by the compiler, not in the archetype). Base text K = G (Cotton Nero A I f. 41, c. 1070); N = A (Harley 55, c. 1050); D (CCCC 201 p. 46, c. 1060) is also given here. II Eg is the ecclesiastical half, III Eg the secular half, of the Andover code (959–c. 962).</note>
      </div>
    </body>
